
     ****************
****** Text::BibTeX ******************************************************
     ****************

Alberto would like to thank you:

* Greg Ward for his work on btparse and Text::BibTeX. He is not
  maintaining this code anymore but without his work none of these
  software packages were possible.

* Philip Kime for his continuous support on my work when porting from
  0.38 to 0.40

* Jens Rehsack and Jerome Quelin for building patchs.


Version 1.00 rewrote the C library at the core of Text::BibTeX, but it
is still Greg Ward's btparse underneath: its design, its grammar, its
rules for splitting and formatting names and processing strings, and
most of its documentation come from btparse, which Greg wrote and
maintained from 1996 to 2000 as part of btOOL.  The library now lives
in src/ and is no longer distributed separately, but the credit and the
LGPL licence (src/COPYING) remain his.
